  "Question": "For a real number \\(x\\), what type of condition is “\\(x>0\\)” for “\\(x>2\\)”?",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "Sufficient but not necessary",
    "B": "Necessary and sufficient",
    "C": "Necessary but not sufficient",
    "D": "Neither sufficient nor necessary"
  },
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Accepted Answers": [],
  "Unordered Answers": false,
  "Solution": "\\(x>2\\) requires \\(x>0\\), so it is necessary. Knowing only that \\(x>0\\) does not imply \\(x>2\\), so it is not sufficient.",
